--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Beken Armino SDK overlay — external/bk_avdk_smp/
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

external/bk_avdk_smp/ is not a copy of the Beken SDK.  It holds the 59 managed
paths this port changes, checked byte-for-byte against a pinned upstream
baseline by external/prepare.sh and recorded in external/manifest.tsv.

  Upstream    https://github.com/bekencorp/bk_avdk_smp.git
  Baseline    d2ded037798530175e5dc5cde6fa1878f5d5ef35

Those files remain Beken's, under the terms Beken ships them with, and are not
restamped with this product's license -- including the ones whose upstream copy
carries no license header.  The changes themselves are ours and are described
in docs/ and in the commit history rather than in per-file headers, because the
digest in external/manifest.tsv exists precisely to keep that tree tracking
upstream byte-for-byte.

One file in that tree is new rather than modified:

  cp/include/components/ap_console_bridge.h

It is the CP-side interface of the AP console bridge, written for this port and
covered by this product's Apache-2.0 grant.  It carries no SPDX line for the
same reason as the rest of the tree.

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Derived logic
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

Two modules were written by following existing openvela code rather than by
copying it, and say so in their own headers: app/velasight/vs_media.c follows
app/social_cue/social_cue_main.c's capture path and the JPEG segment walk in
app/agent_camera/agent_camera_main.c.  No translation units are shared, so
there is no build dependency in either direction and no additional license
obligation.
